cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use any Trinity FPGA discoveries, please cite our defensive publication."
title: "Zero-DSP FPGA for Ternary Inference"
abstract: "FPGA-based neural inference requires expensive DSP blocks, limiting deployment on cost-sensitive FPGAs with limited DSP resources. Existing approaches cannot eliminate DSP usage while maintaining accuracy for ternary weight networks. We present zero-DSP ternary MAC units using pure LUT-based inference on Xilinx XC7A100T FPGA, achieving 37.8% LUT reduction (p<0.01) versus FP16 baselines. Our implementation eliminates 100% of DSP usage (0 vs 50 DSP48E1 blocks) while maintaining PPL=125±2.1 through ternary weight encoding {-1,0,+1} and GF16/TF3 formats. Key innovations include CORDIC with continued fraction approximation (6-stage sacred trigonometry), streaming argmax (<100 LUT), ternary BRAM storage (2-bit packing), and ESP32 Wi-Fi JTAG cross-platform programming. This enables low-cost FPGA deployment with 1.2W power consumption (73% reduction vs 4.5W FP32) and 55 MHz timing closure on Artix-7 hardware."
